{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b7b24048dc20da50","name":"card_unit_kawanishi_h8k","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_kawanishi_h8k","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"KAWANISHI H8K","text":"Draw a card when you Forecast.\r\nDeployment: Forecast.","flavorText":"The Kawanishi H8K was a large four engine flying boat used by the Imperial Japanese Navy Air Service during WWII. It was designed for long-range maritime patrol, reconnaissance, bombing, and transport missions over the Pacific. The first prototype flew in January 1941, and the type entered service in 1942. A total of 167 aircraft were built from 1941 to 1945. The Allies gave it the reporting name Emily. Early tests showed poor handling on water, but changes to the hull and nose spray strips solved many of these problems. The improved H8K2 became the main version, with more powerful engines, greater fuel capacity, and heavier defensive armament. It carried five 20 mm cannons, five 7.7 mm machine-guns, and could carry torpedoes, bombs, or depth charges. Its range of more than 7,000 kilometers made it useful for ocean patrols far from Japanese bases. The H8K first saw combat in 1942 during Operation K, a second raid on Pearl Harbor on 4 March 1942, which required submarine refuelling at French Frigate Shoals. The attack caused no significant damage due to poor visibility, but showed the aircraft’s unusual reach.","faction":"Japan","type":"bomber","rarity":"Unique","cost":6,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":8},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.forecast"],"Name":"card_unit_kawanishi_h8k","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_kawanishi_h8k_title","SourceString":"KAWANISHI H8K","LocalizedString":"KAWANISHI H8K"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":3,"defense":8,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_kawanishi_h8k_text","SourceString":"Draw a card when you Forecast.\r\nDeployment: Forecast.","LocalizedString":"Draw a card when you Forecast.\r\nDeployment: Forecast."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_kawanishi_h8k_history","SourceString":"The Kawanishi H8K was a large four engine flying boat used by the Imperial Japanese Navy Air Service during WWII. It was designed for long-range maritime patrol, reconnaissance, bombing, and transport missions over the Pacific. The first prototype flew in January 1941, and the type entered service in 1942. A total of 167 aircraft were built from 1941 to 1945. The Allies gave it the reporting name Emily. Early tests showed poor handling on water, but changes to the hull and nose spray strips solved many of these problems. The improved H8K2 became the main version, with more powerful engines, greater fuel capacity, and heavier defensive armament. It carried five 20 mm cannons, five 7.7 mm machine-guns, and could carry torpedoes, bombs, or depth charges. Its range of more than 7,000 kilometers made it useful for ocean patrols far from Japanese bases. The H8K first saw combat in 1942 during Operation K, a second raid on Pearl Harbor on 4 March 1942, which required submarine refuelling at French Frigate Shoals. The attack caused no significant damage due to poor visibility, but showed the aircraft’s unusual reach.","LocalizedString":"The Kawanishi H8K was a large four engine flying boat used by the Imperial Japanese Navy Air Service during WWII. It was designed for long-range maritime patrol, reconnaissance, bombing, and transport missions over the Pacific. The first prototype flew in January 1941, and the type entered service in 1942. A total of 167 aircraft were built from 1941 to 1945. The Allies gave it the reporting name Emily. Early tests showed poor handling on water, but changes to the hull and nose spray strips solved many of these problems. The improved H8K2 became the main version, with more powerful engines, greater fuel capacity, and heavier defensive armament. It carried five 20 mm cannons, five 7.7 mm machine-guns, and could carry torpedoes, bombs, or depth charges. Its range of more than 7,000 kilometers made it useful for ocean patrols far from Japanese bases. The H8K first saw combat in 1942 during Operation K, a second raid on Pearl Harbor on 4 March 1942, which required submarine refuelling at French Frigate Shoals. The attack caused no significant damage due to poor visibility, but showed the aircraft’s unusual reach."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardForecasted","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Forecast"],"hasDeployment":true,"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/KAWANISHI_H8K.KAWANISHI_H8K","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_kawanishi_h8k_photo","SourceString":"A Kawanishi H8K2 Flying Boat ashore. Date unknown. ","LocalizedString":"A Kawanishi H8K2 Flying Boat ashore. Date unknown. "},"blowUpExplosion":{"ObjectName":"ParticleSystem'P_ExplosionAircraftM'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Explosions/Medium/Aircraft/P_ExplosionAircraftM.193"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeMedium_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeMedium.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackBomber.BP_AttackBomber_C","SubPathString":""},"isRemoval":true},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_kawanishi_h8k","owner":"card_unit_kawanishi_h8k_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_IsLocatedOnBoard_isIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Draw